# Promptstack design rules

Official brand:
- font: Eurostile, using owner-supplied licensed webfont files
- purple: #A800E6
- navy: #1B263B
- grey: #919191
- lavender: #CBAED3
- white: #FFFFFF

Visual direction:
- light
- premium
- modern
- editorial
- technical
- African
- human
- restrained

Use navy as the dominant text/dark surface.
Use purple as a controlled accent, not a dominant page background.
Use lavender for soft surfaces and Academy accents.
Do not use #919191 for small body text on white; it lacks sufficient normal-text contrast.

Desktop header:
- horizontal navigation
- no hamburger at normal desktop width
- official logo left
- Solutions, Work, How We Work, Academy, Insights, Company
- visible Start a Project CTA right
- Solutions uses a mega-menu
- sticky header
- no giant pill navbar

Avoid:
- neon AI aesthetics
- robots/brains/circuit heads
- purple overload
- template-like card walls
- glassmorphism everywhere
- huge corner radii on everything
- gratuitous parallax
- auto-playing heavy hero video
- hidden desktop navigation

Use CSS-first motion; use a motion library only for interactions that genuinely need it.
Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
